# L §7.6 item 3 (tally 2.1.6, issue #89): a key offset k - n and its pos(k) > n guard have at most 18 digits;
# 1000000000000000000 has 19: LOAD-LIMIT. tally 2.1.5's refcore loaded it (the guard never holds).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = 1..3
input step: int

def x[k in ks]: int at reader
  rule base = step
  rule a beats base = x[k - 1000000000000000000] + step when pos(k) > 1000000000000000000

version v
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  step = 1 "plan"

ask q: x[3] law 2026-06-30
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LIMIT 1000000000000000000 has more than 18 digits (m.tally:14)
